{"id": "EUVD-2026-101059", "enisaUuid": "09eb5361-9be3-36f8-a260-001ddd88d2cf", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwatchdog: da9063: fix suspend/resume handling of HW_RUNNING watchdog\n\nda9063_wdt_suspend() and da9063_wdt_resume() only check watchdog_active(),\nwhen the watchdog is left running by the driver sets\nWDOG_HW_RUNNING in da9063_wdt_probe() but userspace never opens the\ndevice, so WDOG_ACTIVE remains cleared, the wdt_disable() will not be\nexecuted in da9063_wdt_suspend. In this case, the suspend callback is\na no-op and the watchdog keeps counting during system suspend,\nleading to an unexpected system reset.\nCheck WDOG_HW_RUNNING and wdd\uff0ccan fix this issue.", "datePublished": "2026-10-14T13:27:43", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:19:04", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/95adc37f47cdf5a5285f7163b24243680af510be", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c30b419c7e6fbe31c48a44c828174168b732dc5b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1c42e39b0990371b9d76ae22c3f33eb6df341251", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/960d1c85381bcaae866dd799b1c905ec5d39ebce", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1db134d0d2a51a136296584854570e5e04adedb0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7cb575b71ab98194d2e040bded3a7281e089c5ed"], "aliases": ["GHSA-v9jm-64rh-hf94", "CVE-2026-98410"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.22, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "05a6802f-42d3-38e5-94bd-b46ea99582e6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "0b0ecdb9-cd0d-3d39-8c6c-9bfd33fd27b5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "0b5904e1-57e0-3e4a-88fa-09ee8fb97f37", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a7ceca4398bc835c6ad29d10e1106de4cf0332e1 <c30b419c7e6fbe31c48a44c828174168b732dc5b"}, {"id": "105ee3be-c755-3f60-ba61-b2088f41ea9a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendo